//! systema-sysh-console — System H, the boot-log console frontend.
//!
//! Listens on the notify channel for unit start completions and prints one
//! line per unit that reached a terminal start state:
//!
//! ```text
//! [      4821] sshd.service OK [      4903]
//! ```
//!
//! The notify channel has no subscription model (see `sysa::notify`): every
//! event is a datagram broadcast by System A to *every* socket file in the
//! notify directory (`/run/systema/notify`).  There is nothing to connect
//! to — a listener exists by binding its own socket path, which is what
//! this frontend does (`<notify-dir>/console.sock`).  Binding fails until
//! System A has created the directory, so the frontend retries every
//! [`RETRY_INTERVAL`] and stays quiet while it does: a warning per attempt
//! would flood the very console it is meant to write to.
