这两件事逻辑上分开，建议两个提交。功能部分：

```
feat(sysr,syss,sysa): Stop services through their unit cgroup.

System S asks System A where a unit's cgroup lives right before stopping it;
System A relays the question to the resource worker (filling Slice= from the
parsed unit model) and ships the answer back verbatim, so the stop can signal
the whole unit cgroup on top of the main process group and collect children
that escaped it.  Without a resource worker System A answers
`available = false` immediately and the old process-group teardown runs, so
the dependency stays optional.

Stop calls also leave the worker reader loop (their answer can only arrive
through it), every service gets a process group of its own — with TTY units
staying on the setsid() path, since the two mechanisms cannot share a child —
and every probe degrades to pid-based signalling when the cgroup filesystem
says nothing.
```

